# Multi-machine activity log: staff on different machines append rows to the
# same CSV. The git "union" merge driver keeps BOTH machines' lines whenever
# they sync at the same time (no conflict markers, no lost rows).
logs/activity-log.csv merge=union

# logs/.boot-id is PER-MACHINE state (fresh GUID per START-ADMIN) but it is
# tracked in the repo - early commits beat .gitignore to it, and untracking
# it on 2026-10-18 was immediately undone by an old sync engine on another
# machine. It used to be the single file that deadlocked cross-machine sync
# ("Sync stopped: Merge conflict in logs/.boot-id"): every machine rewrites
# it, so every diverging rebase collided, and machines that piled up more
# than 5 conflicted log commits could never get through. The union driver
# keeps both machines' ids and needs no conflict handling at all - and
# because a rebase checks out upstream's .gitattributes first (and log
# commits never modify that file), even machines still running the OLD
# sync engine get conflict-free merges. The app adopts whatever the file
# says, so a merged file only forces a staff re-pick when it next changes.
logs/.boot-id merge=union
